  "note": "Annual election of the Antrim Town Commissioners, polled Tuesday 15 January 1929. Only nine nominations were received for the nine vacancies, so all were returned unopposed (Belfast News-Letter, 7 January 1929, p. 4). Four old members (Cooper, Carson, M'Cabe, Wilson) and five new (Barr, Beggs, Erskine, Lawlor, Millar). Returned unopposed."
